<http://data.silknow.org/object/235adfff-4054-30aa-bf12-f2ed8c98fab0>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Silk bag face, double cloth, with four widthways repeat of design which is picked out in cream silk on an oyster-coloured ground. Three lengthwise repeats of an ogee compartmentalised design enclosing buttercup-like clumps of flowers surrounded by trailing acanthus leaves and meandering flowering plants.\n\nThe fabric structure, although a conventional double cloth, is lightweight and woven from two silks, one showing a tusser in its raw unbleached state."@en , "Silk bag face, probably made by Alexander Morton & Co., Darvel, Scotland, ca. 1890"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/c112389c-2715-3d2d-8350-583ab30b92c5> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Silk bag face, double cloth, with four widthways repeat of design which is picked out in cream silk on an oyster-coloured ground. Three lengthwise repeats of an ogee compartmentalised design enclosing buttercup-like clumps of flowers surrounded by trailing acanthus leaves and meandering flowering plants.\n\nThe fabric structure, although a conventional double cloth, is lightweight and woven from two silks, one showing a tusser in its raw unbleached state."@en , "Silk bag face, probably made by Alexander Morton & Co., Darvel, Scotland, ca. 1890"@en ;
